# Unit tests

Create unit tests for new functionalities, features, stories, and infra. Load `.cursor/skills/add-unit-tests/SKILL.md` when adding tests.

## When tests are mandatory

- New/changed MediatR handler, validator, domain rule, permission policy
- New repository/adapter, JWT/Identity behavior, mapping that encodes rules
- New API story (test the application handler, not the MVC pipeline, unless asked)

UI-only Blazor markup may skip unit tests; extractable client services must be tested.

## No test project yet (Phase 10)

Adding `tests/*.csproj` is an architecture/package change. **Ask once**, propose:

- `tests/ForensicsAnalyzer.Application.Tests` (xUnit, FluentAssertions, NSubstitute, `net9.0`)
- later: Domain, Infrastructure, WebApi as needed

After the user approves, add the project and tests in the same task. After it exists, always add tests without asking.

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — handler/validator in isolation
[Fact]
public async Task Handle_Should_Set_Owner_From_CurrentUser() { /* substitute ports, assert */ }

// ❌ BAD — no test because “small”; or spinning SQL Server for a validator
```

Do not add test packages to production projects. Do not merge new behavior without tests or an explicit user skip.
